WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.463
This video was made by democut.

00:00:02.463 --> 00:00:06.619
You write a short storyboard, your coding agent records the app,

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:09.346
and democut edits it into a narrated demo.

00:00:10.783 --> 00:00:13.221
Here is Taskboard, a tiny sample app.

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:18.229
This is a real browser recording, with a cursor viewers can actually follow.

00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:20.590
First, the shots.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.515
Typing happens at a human pace, and the camera eases in on

00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:26.829
the part that matters.

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:31.163
Every click gets a ripple and a short pause before it,

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.435
so nobody loses track of what happened.

00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:38.425
Page loads are cut out, and slow parts are sped up to

00:00:38.425 --> 00:00:42.095
fit the narration. Each shot lasts as long as its voiceover.

00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.670
Every shot carries a badge that says where it came from.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.513
This chart uses made-up numbers, so it says so.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.648
Email addresses and other private text are masked before the page is

00:00:54.648 --> 00:00:56.903
painted, so they never reach the video.

00:00:58.117 --> 00:00:59.653
Second, how it is made.

00:01:01.117 --> 00:01:04.789
A short Playwright script records the takes, and marks a scene around

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:06.173
each moment worth showing.

00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:09.519
Then one command builds every cut.

00:01:09.519 --> 00:01:12.848
The voice is Kokoro, running offline on your machine,

00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:14.167
so nothing leaves it.

00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:18.003
From one storyboard you get a full cut,

00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:21.026
a short cut, captions, a GIF for your readme,

00:01:21.026 --> 00:01:23.175
and a player page with chapters.

00:01:23.175 --> 00:01:24.451
It is MIT licensed.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:27.138
Install it in Claude Code with one line.

